00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:23.360
[Rebecca] Today, our Kings and Queens of England series examines the tragic, sensitive, and ill-fated sovereign whose reign collapsed under the weight of unrequited expectations, leading to a humiliating defeat at Bannockburn and the first violent deposition of an anointed English king.

4
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.720
[Rebecca] Here is George with the extraordinary story of Edward I.

5
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:41.360
[George] Born in April 1284 at the newly constructed fortress of Cairnarfon in Wales, Edward of Carnarfon was the fourth and only surviving son of Edward I and Alina of Castile.

6
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.840
[George] Handsome, tall, with broad shoulders and athletic physical grace.

7
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.920
[George] Young Edward was an emotional disappointment to his ferocious father.

8
00:00:49.920 --> 00:01:03.280
[George] Where Longshanks was consumed by warfare, law, and conquest, young Edward hated tournaments, preferred the companionship of common craftsmen, and enjoyed music, acting, thatching roofs, and rowing boats.

9
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:11.200
[George] In 1300, his father assigned a witty, flamboyant young Gascon knight named Piers Gaveston to the prince's household.

10
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.320
[George] The bond between Edward and Gaveston was instant, all consuming and passionate.

11
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.080
[George] Chroniclers described their love as beyond the measure of women.

12
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:34.240
[George] When Prince Edward demanded that his father grant Gaveston the hereditary county of Ponthew, old King Edward flew into an apoplectic fury, tearing out handfuls of his son's hair and exiling Gaveston from the realm under pain of death.

13
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:41.840
[George] Growing up as the surviving son of the terrifying, towering Edward Longshanks was an emotional nightmare for young Prince Edward.

14
00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:56.000
[George] Where his father was an iron willed conqueror who spent his life in chainmill, young Edward was an artistic, sensitive soul who preferred digging ditches with laborers, breeding horses, practicing carpentry, and swimming in the Thames.

15
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:07.560
[George] His passionate relationship with Piers Gaveston, a dashing, athletic Gascon knight who possessed supreme skill in the tournament lists, was the defining emotional sanctuary of Edward's life.

16
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:13.000
[George] When old King Edward discovered that Prince Edward had gifted Gaveston royal crown lands.

17
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:25.320
[George] The ferocious old monarch attacked his son in a volcanic rage, tearing out clumps of the prince's hair and banishing Gaveston to France under oath of death, driving a permanent wedge between father and son.

18
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.840
[George] The moment old Longshanks died in July 1307, 23-year-old Edward I.

19
