[George] Gaveston mocked the great magnates with cruel, witty nicknames, calling Thomas of Lancaster, the Churle and the Old Hog, and the Earl of Pembroke, Joseph the Jew.

30
00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:25.120
[George] In 1311, the barons forced Edward to accept the ordinances, banishing Gaveston on pain of excommunication.

31
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:32.880
[George] When King Edward recklessly recalled Gaveston from exile for a third time in late 1311, civil war erupted.

32
00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:44.320
[George] Trapped in Scarborough Castle by baronial forces, Gaveston surrendered to the moderate Earl of Pembroke on the solemn chivalric promise that his life would be spared while negotiations were held.

33
00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:55.040
