[George] King Robert the Bruce, commanding a smaller Scottish army of six thousand spearmen, deployed his dense, hedgehog like shiltrons on the firm ground bordering the waterlogged Bannockburn marsh.

51
00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.200
[George] Edward's generalship was disastrously incompetent.

52
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:57.840
[George] He crammed his heavy cavalry into a narrow bottleneck between the streams, where English knights were slaughtered in the mud by bristling Scottish spears, unable to charge or retreat.

53
