54
00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:24.960
[George] Following the disaster of Bannockburn and the great famine of 1315 that starved thousands of English peasants, Edward found a new and far more dangerous favourite, Hugh Dispenser the Younger, an ambitious, greedy and ruthless marcher lord, alongside his cunning father.

55
00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:35.360
[George] Dispenser dominated the king's affection and bedchamber, using royal patronage to illegally seize vast estates in South Wales and extort wealth from rival nobles.

56
00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:44.240
